# Initial Setup's OSD page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigHWOSD.cs (PLAN.md §13.6
# row 70).
#
# The claim: the page shows the heading, the MinimOSD's box, "Enable Telemetry" and the note
# beside it at the .resx's places, and is enabled whatever the link (ConfigHWOSD.cs:14-21);
# Enable Telemetry sets the 24 stream rates a MinimOSD needs - SR0_, SR1_ and SR3_ each of
# EXT_STAT, EXTRA1-3, POSITION, RAW_CTRL, RAW_SENS and RC_CHAN - to 2 in one try (:23-68), each
# write proved by the vehicle's echo. A failure is a status line, not the C#'s box (the owner's
# ruling of 2026-09-25).
#
# The page has no way back: this run leaves SITL's SR0, SR1 and SR3 rates at 2, as Mission
# Planner's would; a fresh SITL puts them back.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-osd.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000

click tab-setup
expect config.osd.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigHWOSD
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigHWOSD
expect config.osd.active true
expect config.osd.enabled true
expect config.osd.heading OSD
expect config.osd.button Enable Telemetry
expect config.osd.note You only need to use this if you are having issue with your OSD not updating
expect config.osd.write none
expect config.osd.presses 0

click osd-enable-telemetry
settle 12
expect config.osd.presses 1
expect config.osd.writes.pending 0
expect config.osd.write SR3_RC_CHAN 2 accepted
expect config.osd.message none
expect params.value.SR0_EXT_STAT 2
expect params.value.SR1_EXTRA1 2
expect params.value.SR3_RC_CHAN 2

# Choosing another page hides this one; it is IActivate only.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect config.osd.active false
